On-the-job training as part of a committed customer focused team;
Regular feedback from Mentors; Work-readiness training and development.
Requirements
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS
A completed Matric qualification;
Must have successfully completed at least one of the following qualifications, with an overall average of 70% achieved;
Higher National Certificate or National Diploma in Occupational Health and Safety, BHSc Occupational Hygiene or Bachelor of Environmental Health with occupational hygiene.
DOCUMENT TO SUBMIT WHEN UPLOADING YOUR APPLICATION
2 page CV;
Certified copy of your ID document;
Certified copy of your Matric qualification;
Certified copies of both your academic record and qualification (s);
Kindly complete a MS Excel spreadsheet that will be used to confirm your aggregate achieved cumulatively over the years of study. Please ensure that it is also attached as part of your application. Please note that any applications that do not accompany this MS Excel document will not be considered.
The following are the guidelines for completing the MS Excel spreadsheet:
Step 1—Add ALL module names (courses) and percentages achieved for qualifications attained (i.e. ALL module percentages for National Diploma + BTech./Advanced Diploma + Honours/ Postgraduate Diploma + Masters Degree/ MTech);
Step 2—Count the number of modules you have completed throughout ALL tertiary qualifications attained;
Step 3—Sum of ALL modules completed divided by number of modules completed will then give you your total aggregate.
