This dynamic role will be perfect for an individual who is looking to pursue a career within the retail industry or someone who values strategic planning and problem solving, customer satisfaction, and working in an innovative environment.
With a starting Cost to Company of between R12 000 and R20 000 per month, we're looking for people who value strategic planning, problem-solving, customer satisfaction and working in an innovative environment.
What would the job entail?
As a Category Planner at DotActiv you would be responsible for :
(By utilising DotActiv's Category Planning Software)
Creating strategic assortment plans;
Designing data-driven floor space plans;
Planning and building data-driven shelf plans;
Conducting floor and space plan analytical reviews;
Developing optimised cluster plans per product category using the cluster optimizer and maintenance tools in the DotActiv software;
Analysing the cluster plan and profiling each cluster to deliver strategic insights to clients;
Maximising customer and category performance by considering category strategies and plans, product financial performance, shopper psychology and aesthetic appeal; and
Supporting, advising and guiding retail customers where required
Requirements
Creative flair and ability to identify aesthetic/visual appeal
2+ years of similar and relevant experience in the Retail Sector
Strong Interpersonal Skills
Computer Literacy - MS Office
Driver's license and own transport
Strong verbal and written communication skills (English)
Team player
Strong organisational and prioritisation skills
Self-motivated and results oriented
Must have strong analytical skills and be able to use data analysis techniques and how to apply these to business situations;
You must have a high capacity to represent the DotActiv brand as a specialist;
You must have a high degree of internal client engagement;
Consumer Science, Business/Marketing or Supply Chain related degree is a must
Benefits
Here's what you can expect from DotActiv when joining the team as a Category Planner.
You'll receive a Cost to Company of between R12k and R20k depending on your experience;
You'll have the opportunity to upskill yourself in any field that adds value to your current position;
We offer you a transparent job grading system; and
We offer you a developmental path specific to your circumstances, allowing you to track your progress

Synopsis
The Senior Project Manager will be responsible for three (3) of the seven (7) programmes, SIP, TCP and PEPP. The Senior Project Manager will be accountable for the end-to-end management and continued development of the programmes across Bid Windows; new, active and legacy portfolios.
The role integrates programme strategy and governance, programme entry and grant funding, and programme reporting and financial control.
Operating within a small TCF team, the Senior Project Manager is expected to combine senior judgement and governance accountability with hands-on portfolio control and delivery.
Job Description
MAIN DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Develop and/or refine all aspects of Programme Management (including Bid Windows, project execution and close out) for programmes 5, 6 and 7 (SIP, TCP and PEPP);
Manage contracting and execute tight contracts management controls (incl. all aspects of procurement as required by IDC and/or Board);
Develop and implement operational systems, processes and procedures for efficient management of the Fund:
Develop and implement suitable processes and systems to conduct pragmatic project and programme monitoring and reporting;
Manage the Consultants to the technical work streams, including:
Set and agree performance targets for all obligations;
Define and conclude contracts and/or other agreements (e.g. Service-level agreements), scrutinise submitted payment certificates before recommending for signature by the CEO and subsequent payment by the IDC, for selected beneficiaries of funding under programmes and based on achievement of contractual milestones;
Conduct site visits and provide leadership in investigations, ensuring the implementation of all site technical, quality, health and safety protocols to prevent incidents and ensuring that projects are delivered on time, within budget, required quality and without incident;
Conduct site team reviews, identify trends and ensure action on all non-conformances;
Ensure proper close-outs of project (formally) and write and distribute the report with lessons learnt, ensuring that all costs and outstanding issues are concluded.
Contribute to the Annual Plan and Annual Report as well as any other reports required by the Trustees and the CEO, for stakeholders;
Ensure legal and financial (incl. auditing) compliance with the relevant legislation;
In support of the CEO, draft reports and executive submissions as required by the IDC, relevant ministries and Trustees for its annual planning and business processes;
Occasionally review the Operational Guidelines adopted by the Trustees and recommend amendments, to ensure more focused and efficient processes and evaluation criteria for each of the Programmes;
Co-ordinate activities of all the internal IDC departments involved with the Trust, the dtic and other key stakeholders.
Qualification and Experience
QUALIFICATIONS
Professionally qualified engineer, quantity surveyor or another construction-related professional field;
Professional registration will be an advantaged.
Registration as a Project Management Professionals (PMP) or Construction Management Professionals (SACPCMP) will be an advantage;
Post Graduate Qualifications will be an advantage (e.g. an MEng/MBA/MBL).
KNOWLEDGE & EXPERIENCE
8 to 10 years’ experience within the built environment
All aspects of construction and built-environment activities;
Senior management, preferably also in private sector (e.g. a construction company) would be an advantage;
Project and risk management;
Managing or overseeing social infrastructure projects; and
Dealing with communities, municipalities, provincial and national government.
Roles and Responsibilities
TECHNICAL/FUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES
Technical Construction Project Management expertise;
Competent to provide inputs in the adjudication of construction tenders;
Infrastructure monitoring and management experience and expertise;
Competent in Project Risk management;
Business management competence (including private sector);
The ability to lead teams to get projects through conceptualisation and construction;
The ability to do root cause analysis and interventions for projects in distress;
The ability to work as an individual, but also in a complex team environment;
Roles and Responsibilities (cont.)
BEHAVIOURAL COMPETENCIES
High professional integrity, sound judgement and strong governance ethics.
Strategic and systems thinking combined with practical delivery discipline.
Analytical, decisive and comfortable managing ambiguity, competing priorities and distressed situations.
Strong leadership, negotiation, communication and stakeholder-management capability.
Able to work independently and collaboratively in a small, multidisciplinary team.
Commercially pragmatic while maintaining the developmental objectives and fiduciary responsibilities of the Fund.
Impeccable technical report writing skills, with attention to detail.
Posting End Date
02 Oct 2026

Detailed description:
The successful candidate will be responsible for the following key performance areas:
Prepare and provide accurate and reliable data and information in support of strategic decisions.
Acquire new data sources to enable effective departmental decision-making.
Create and maintain consistent metadata in a manner that allows for clear and
unambiguous data definitions and meets legislative, quality and security requirements.
Create and maintain business metadata for published data sources to ensure they are easily discoverable and meaningful to information consumers.
Prepare relevant data for appropriate consumers in the SARB Group and relevant stakeholders, and monitor published data sources for usage, relevance and quality feedback.
Ensure that assigned data elements are current, do not conflict with other data elements in the metadata registry and are used consistently across various systems.
Proactively identify and resolve data integrity and quality issues.
Stay current with developments in all functional areas relevant to information management and ensure their appropriate application.
Propose and implement refinements and continuous improvements to systems, tools, methods and processes in own area.
