a bachelor's degree in either information technology, computer science or mathematics, or an equivalent NQF 7 qualification in a related field;
five to eight years' experience in any of the relevant data management disciplines, such as data governance, metadata management, master data management, business intelligence and data development; and
relevant certifications, such as Certified Data Steward, will be an advantage.
Additional requirements include:
knowledge and skills in:
reference and master data;
metadata management; and
data quality management;
service and stakeholder focus;
effective communication;
impact and influence;
drive for results;
problem-solving and analysis;
planning and organising;
innovation and creativity;
judgement and decision-making; and
conceptual thinking.
